 "caption": "Energy-error order test on the production system (N = 1000, \u03b7 = 0.35, 20+/20\u2212, l_B = 5 \u03c3): maximum |E(t) \u2212 E(0)|/N over 2 \u03c4 of NVE dynamics versus the step h for the four integrators, with the fitted log\u2013log slopes in the legends and dashed reference lines \u221d h and \u221d h\u00b2. (a) Equilibrated start (15 \u03c4 with charges on): the shipped cv-phys is second order (slope 2.02) whereas the literal HLL collision Verlet is only sub-first-order (slope 0.73) and 35\u00d7 less accurate at the production step h = 0.005 \u03c4; kdk-phys gives 1.82 and the naive splitting 1.09. (b) Same test from the un-equilibrated start with Ewald (solid; slopes 1.40 / 0.78 / 1.69 / 0.89) and with the smooth DSF Coulomb model (dashed, cv-phys 1.92, cv 1.21). The Ewald real-space truncation erfc(\u03b1r_c) \u2248 7.5\u00d710\u207b\u2075 gives an energy floor of \u2248 0.5\u20131 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2076 kT/N that limits the cv-phys curve at h = 0.0025 \u03c4 (local slope 1.0 between 0.005 and 0.0025 \u03c4; 6 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2077 kT/N in (a)); cv and naive are flat there because of their own first-order collision error (65\u00d7 and 229\u00d7 above the floor, local slopes 0.11 and \u22120.06), and kdk-phys is not yet affected (local slope 2.9).",
